# drivers/TegraGM20BMetal on the host:
#   raw_target_test   raw/runtime/raw_target.h: the raw path's color target words, pitch as before and a mip chain's level as
#                     NVK's block-linear target, addressing every texel where raw/fx's layout (the texture header's and
#                     the 2D engine's view of the chain) has it
#   raw_layout_test   drivers/TegraGM20B/TegraGM20BLayout.h: the block-linear layout every GPU user takes is NIL's (its
#                     answers for one-level images of every texel size), raw/fx's level 0 and the display's tiled scan
#   nvk_wait_any_test nvkmd_darwin's WAIT_ANY (nvkmd_darwin_wait_any.h) over a model of the kext's WaitFence: it returns
#                     once one sync of the set resolves (a host signal, a fence's interrupt), sleeps until then, keeps
#                     its deadline, and calls a passed fence whose wake never came a lost interrupt
#   nvk_kill_test     nvkmd_darwin's view of a channel the kernel killed (nvkmd_darwin_kill.h): the fence word's kill record
#                     names the seqnos that never ran, a kept record answers for its old channel alone, a timeline keeps
#                     its failed values
#   nvk_surfaces_test nvkmd_darwin's ExecSurfaces record (nvkmd_darwin_surfaces.h): each BO once with its accesses merged,
#                     past its room the all-imports flag, its length
#   raw_events_source_test  how a command buffer with a plain or shared Metal event stays raw (frontend, bridge, m2v,
#                     RawMetal), and the cross-process shared event refusal line
#   raw_follow_test   raw/runtime/raw_follow.h: the raw path's threads take a fixed-priority committer's policy, never a
#                     lower one, and keep their own for a timeshare committer
#   raw_tiled_cache_test  raw/runtime/raw_tiled_cache.h: with the kernel's tiled-cache bit, deko3d's configuration then the
#                     enable at context init and one flush per command buffer; nothing without it
#   raw_comp_test     raw/runtime/raw_comp.h: the compressible kinds the raw path binds are the kernel kind table's (nouveau
#                     gm200_mmu_kind) and demote as it says; the boot ZBC values read alike by Metal and NV format
#   stage_test        stage-tegra-gm20b-metal.py on a directory standing in for the Data volume
#   raw_ycbcr_test    raw/runtime/raw_ycbcr.cpp: the two-plane YCbCr textures the raw path converts (m2v's rules) and the
#                     conversion's shape; its texels against Metal's reads are raw/test/ycbcroracle.mm's (this Mac's GPU)
#   raw_xr_test       raw/runtime/raw_xr.h: the extended-range formats the raw path keeps and the codes Metal's Clear
#                     stores in them (an M4 Max's); against Metal's own reads and clears it is raw/test/xroracle.mm's
#   raw_clear_test    raw/runtime/raw_clear.h: the clear values the raw path hands NVK, m2v's for every format it renders
#                     (raw/test/targetcheck.py: its target formats against NVK's)
#   raw_sampler_test  raw/runtime/raw_sampler.h: the Metal samplers the raw path takes, as m2v samples them on NVK
#                     (raw/test/samplercheck: their headers against NVK's)
#   raw_cache_test    raw/runtime/raw_cache.h: the records the runtime makes for states the pack lacks, kept on disk and
#                     made once per process (raw/test/cachecheck: the same checks on a bucket's real records), and
#                     raw_metallib.h: the functions' AIR hashes that key them
#   raw_bounds_test   raw/runtime/raw_bounds.h: a Core Animation draw's pixel box and rectangle from its vertices (against
#                     a GPU's coverage it is raw/test/boundsoracle.mm's, this Mac's GPU), and raw_region.h: the fetch
#                     barrier's region test over such draws, and which covers a render area (a clear it makes redundant)
#   raw_overlap_test  raw/runtime/raw_overlap.h: a fetching draw's triangles in runs that share no pixel (against a GPU's
#                     coverage it is raw/test/overlaporacle.mm's, this Mac's GPU)
#   nak_half_round_test  NAK's rewrites of metal2vulkan's half emulation (nak_nir_algebraic.py): its rounding as two
#                     conversions, the same for every f32 input; half sums and products in f32 as HADD2/HMUL2, the
#                     same for every pair of halves
#
#   bazel test //drivers/TegraGM20BMetal/test:all
